# Script obligations

Duties the complete script H2 owner population satisfies across its execution-ready handoff to screenplay. Each item appears one or more times across that population, as its wording requires. They permit no exclusion.

## Release partition {#release-partition}

Place every delivery-group, unit-file, sequence, scene, and beat boundary where the part an audience receives is whole on its own. A unit ends by leaving the audience holding something that the next unit answers; a delivery group closes where the film has turned, not where a count happens to end.

A boundary that only interrupts is not a release partition. Cutting in the middle of a progression can raise arousal without increasing willingness to continue, so test what the break actually leaves with the audience.

Review question: where does each delivery boundary leave a whole part and a specific pressure, question, consequence, or formal state for the next part, and which boundary merely interrupts?

This obligation owns only where the division falls. Audience investment owns unit-level attention, narrative unit-addressability owns independent progression within an addressable unit, and common proportionate development owns how much development each unit receives.

Sources: [Warhol on how instalment publication alters attention, interpretation, and form](https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/victorian-literature-and-culture/article/seriality/8973016E70A446AB823B4094175F5655); [Digital Dickens Notes Project on discrete serial composition, installment constraints, and whole-pattern pressure](https://dickensnotes.org/introduction/scholarly); [Wirz and colleagues on cliffhangers raising arousal without increasing continuation intention](https://doi.org/10.1037/ppm0000392).

## Script boundary {#script-boundary}

Across the complete script population, settle every physical progression and consequential exchange required for screenplay while leaving final audience wording, visual and aural selection, camera and lighting grammar, editorial mapping, exact shot-owned time, representation construction, and source interpolation to the contracts that own them.

Review question: could a screenplay author refine the complete script population without inventing essential physical progression, and which script sentence would have to move downward because it chooses final presentation or implementation?

Sources: [Plan-and-Write on separating planning from realization](https://doi.org/10.1609/aaai.v33i01.33017378); [NASA systems engineering handbook on allocation and traceability](https://www.nasa.gov/reference/systems-engineering-handbook/)
